      <title>175 years ago, the world's first medical college for women graduated its inaugural class in Philly</title>
      <link>https://www.phillyvoice.com/philly-firsts-medical-college-women/?utm_source=pv-rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=pv-site</link>
      <description>The Woman’s Medical College of Pennsylvania, established by a group of Quakers in Philadelphia in 1850, was the first degree-granting medical school in the world for women. It's among several 'firsts' being celebrate in Philly this March.</description>
